<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Pretrain Results on 7B-Parameter Models</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To further verify the effectiveness of GPAS on larger scale models, we perform pretraining experiments on Pre-LN and Pre + GPAS with 7B parameters. We follow <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">41</a>]</cite> and use a learning rate of <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3\times 10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\times 10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math> with 10K warmup steps and cosine decay. Batch size is set to 2048 and scheduled to train for 150K steps on 60B tokens. We use gradient clipping of <math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.01</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.01</annotation></semantics></math> on gate parameters <math id="A1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.0</annotation></semantics></math> on other parameters to stabilize training. Due to constraints on computational resources, we only train the models up to 40K steps with 16B tokens. After 40K training steps, Pre-LN and Pre + GPAS reached evaluation perplexity of 15.27 and 13.82, respectively. As shown in Figure <a href="#A1.F8.sf2" title="In Figure 8 ‣ Appendix A Pretrain Results on 7B-Parameter Models ‣ GPAS: Accelerating Convergence of LLM Pretraining via Gradient-Preserving Activation Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8(b)</span></a>, Pre + GPAS achieves a much faster convergence than vanilla Pre-LN.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.F8" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A1.F8.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2506.22049v1/7b_pretrain_loss.svg" id="A1.F8.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/228;" width="476" height="228"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A1.F8.sf1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(a)</span> </span><span id="A1.F8.sf1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Pretrain loss</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A1.F8.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2506.22049v1/7b_eval_loss.svg" id="A1.F8.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/228;" width="476" height="228"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A1.F8.sf2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(b)</span> </span><span id="A1.F8.sf2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Evaluation loss</span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A1.F8.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 8</span>: </span><span id="A1.F8.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Pretrain and evaluation loss of Pre-LN and Pre + GPAS, 7B parameters</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Gradient Preservation with GPAS</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Following Section <a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 Pre-LN with GPAS ‣ 3 Gradient-Preserving Activation Scaling ‣ GPAS: Accelerating Convergence of LLM Pretraining via Gradient-Preserving Activation Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>, the gradient <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial\mathcal{L}/\partial x_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em">/</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial\mathcal{L}/\partial x_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\text{naive scaling:}\quad\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial x_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>naive scaling:</mtext><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{naive scaling:}\quad\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial x_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial x_{L}}\prod_{l=1}^{L-1}\frac{\partial x_{l+1}}{\partial x_{l}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial x_{L}}\prod_{l=1}^{L-1}\frac{\partial x_{l+1}}{\partial x_{l}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial x_{L}}\prod_{l=1}^{L-1}\left(\frac{\partial x_{l+1}}{\partial x_{l+1}^{\prime}}\frac{\partial x_{l+1}^{\prime}}{\partial x_{l}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial x_{L}}\prod_{l=1}^{L-1}\left(\frac{\partial x_{l+1}}{\partial x_{l+1}^{\prime}}\frac{\partial x_{l+1}^{\prime}}{\partial x_{l}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial x_{L}}\prod_{l=1}^{L-1}\frac{\partial x_{l+1}^{\prime}}{\partial x_{l}}\cdot\prod_{l=1}^{L-1}\frac{\partial x_{l+1}}{\partial x_{l+1}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial x_{L}}\prod_{l=1}^{L-1}\frac{\partial x_{l+1}^{\prime}}{\partial x_{l}}\cdot\prod_{l=1}^{L-1}\frac{\partial x_{l+1}}{\partial x_{l+1}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial x_{L}}\prod_{l=1}^{L-1}\frac{\partial x_{l+1}^{\prime}}{\partial x_{l}}\cdot\prod_{l=1}^{L-1}\beta_{l}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial x_{L}}\prod_{l=1}^{L-1}\frac{\partial x_{l+1}^{\prime}}{\partial x_{l}}\cdot\prod_{l=1}^{L-1}\beta_{l},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\text{GPAS{}:}\quad\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial x_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>GPAS:</mtext><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{GPAS{}:}\quad\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial x_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial x_{L}}\prod_{l=1}^{L-1}\frac{\partial x_{l+1}^{\prime}}{\partial x_{l}}\cdot\prod_{l=1}^{L-1}\frac{\partial x_{l+1}}{\partial x_{l+1}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial x_{L}}\prod_{l=1}^{L-1}\frac{\partial x_{l+1}^{\prime}}{\partial x_{l}}\cdot\prod_{l=1}^{L-1}\frac{\partial x_{l+1}}{\partial x_{l+1}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial x_{L}}\prod_{l=1}^{L-1}\frac{\partial x_{l+1}^{\prime}}{\partial x_{l}}\cdot\prod_{l=1}^{L-1}I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial x_{L}}\prod_{l=1}^{L-1}\frac{\partial x_{l+1}^{\prime}}{\partial x_{l}}\cdot\prod_{l=1}^{L-1}I</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial x_{L}}\prod_{l=1}^{L-1}\frac{\partial x_{l+1}^{\prime}}{\partial x_{l}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial x_{L}}\prod_{l=1}^{L-1}\frac{\partial x_{l+1}^{\prime}}{\partial x_{l}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Variance and Gradient Growth in Pre-LN with GPAS). ‣ 5.6 Gradient Analysis ‣ 5 Analysis ‣ GPAS: Accelerating Convergence of LLM Pretraining via Gradient-Preserving Activation Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> of GPAS</h2>

<div id="A3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">By equation (<a href="#S3.E1" title="In 3.1 Pre-LN with GPAS ‣ 3 Gradient-Preserving Activation Scaling ‣ GPAS: Accelerating Convergence of LLM Pretraining via Gradient-Preserving Activation Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) and <a href="#S3.E2" title="In 3.1 Pre-LN with GPAS ‣ 3 Gradient-Preserving Activation Scaling ‣ GPAS: Accelerating Convergence of LLM Pretraining via Gradient-Preserving Activation Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, we have the following:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A3.E13X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E13X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle y</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E13X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=x_{\ell+1}=x^{\prime}_{\ell}+\mathrm{FFN}(\frac{1}{\sqrt{\ell}}\mathrm{LN}(x^{\prime}_{\ell}))," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>FFN</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>LN</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=x_{\ell+1}=x^{\prime}_{\ell}+\mathrm{FFN}(\frac{1}{\sqrt{\ell}}\mathrm{LN}(x^{\prime}_{\ell})),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.E13Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E13Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x^{\prime}_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x^{\prime}_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E13Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=x_{\ell}+\mathrm{Attn}(\frac{1}{\sqrt{\ell}}\mathrm{LN}(x_{\ell}))." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>Attn</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>LN</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=x_{\ell}+\mathrm{Attn}(\frac{1}{\sqrt{\ell}}\mathrm{LN}(x_{\ell})).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E14.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\text{Pre-LN:}~x_{l+1}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Pre-LN:</mtext><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{Pre-LN:}~x_{l+1}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=x_{l}+f(\mathrm{LN}(x_{l})),\quad f\in\{\mathrm{Attn},\mathrm{FFN}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>LN</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>Attn</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>FFN</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=x_{l}+f(\mathrm{LN}(x_{l})),\quad f\in\{\mathrm{Attn},\mathrm{FFN}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\text{+ GPAS{}:}~x_{l+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>+ GPAS:</mtext><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{+ GPAS{}:}~x_{l+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=x_{l+1}^{\prime}-\mathrm{SiLU}(\alpha_{l})\cdot\mathrm{sg}(x_{l+1}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>SiLU</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>sg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=x_{l+1}^{\prime}-\mathrm{SiLU}(\alpha_{l})\cdot\mathrm{sg}(x_{l+1}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Following the variance analysis in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>]</cite>, both the <math id="A3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{FFN}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>FFN</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{FFN}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Attn}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Attn</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Attn}</annotation></semantics></math> modules contribute equally to variance accumulation. For simplicity, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A3.E16X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E16X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sigma^{2}_{x_{\ell+1}}=\sigma_{x_{\ell}}^{2}(1+\frac{1}{\sigma_{x_{\ell}}})\cdot(1-\mathrm{SiLU}(\alpha_{l}))." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>SiLU</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sigma^{2}_{x_{\ell+1}}=\sigma_{x_{\ell}}^{2}(1+\frac{1}{\sigma_{x_{\ell}}})\cdot(1-\mathrm{SiLU}(\alpha_{l})).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">The variance with regard to <math id="A3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{x_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{x_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A3.E17X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E17X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sigma^{2}_{x_{\ell}}=\sigma_{x_{1}}^{2}\Theta\Big(\prod^{\ell-1}_{k=1}\Big(1+\frac{1}{\sigma_{x_{k}}}\Big)\Big(1-\mathrm{SiLU}(\alpha_{l})\Big)\Big)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>SiLU</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sigma^{2}_{x_{\ell}}=\sigma_{x_{1}}^{2}\Theta\Big(\prod^{\ell-1}_{k=1}\Big(1+\frac{1}{\sigma_{x_{k}}}\Big)\Big(1-\mathrm{SiLU}(\alpha_{l})\Big)\Big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">For the parameter <math id="A3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> we have</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\operatorname{SiLU}(\alpha_{\ell})=1-\frac{\alpha_{\ell}}{1+e^{-\alpha_{\ell}}}=\frac{(1+e^{-\alpha_{\ell}})-\alpha_{\ell}}{1+e^{-\alpha_{\ell}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>SiLU</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\operatorname{SiLU}(\alpha_{\ell})=1-\frac{\alpha_{\ell}}{1+e^{-\alpha_{\ell}}}=\frac{(1+e^{-\alpha_{\ell}})-\alpha_{\ell}}{1+e^{-\alpha_{\ell}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\sigma_{x_{\ell}}^{2}=\log\sigma_{x_{1}}^{2}+\sum_{k=1}^{\ell-1}\log\Bigl(1+\frac{1}{\sigma_{x_{k}}}\Bigr)+\log\Bigl(1-\operatorname{SiLU}(\alpha_{\ell})\Bigr)+C," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>SiLU</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\sigma_{x_{\ell}}^{2}=\log\sigma_{x_{1}}^{2}+\sum_{k=1}^{\ell-1}\log\Bigl(1+\frac{1}{\sigma_{x_{k}}}\Bigr)+\log\Bigl(1-\operatorname{SiLU}(\alpha_{\ell})\Bigr)+C,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> is an (unspecified) constant. Using the original definition for SiLU we have</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\Bigl(1-\operatorname{SiLU}(\alpha_{\ell})\Bigr)=\log\Bigl(\frac{1+e^{-\alpha_{\ell}}-\alpha_{\ell}}{1+e^{-\alpha_{\ell}}}\Bigr)=\log\bigl(1+e^{-\alpha_{\ell}}-\alpha_{\ell}\bigr)-\log\bigl(1+e^{-\alpha_{\ell}}\bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>SiLU</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\Bigl(1-\operatorname{SiLU}(\alpha_{\ell})\Bigr)=\log\Bigl(\frac{1+e^{-\alpha_{\ell}}-\alpha_{\ell}}{1+e^{-\alpha_{\ell}}}\Bigr)=\log\bigl(1+e^{-\alpha_{\ell}}-\alpha_{\ell}\bigr)-\log\bigl(1+e^{-\alpha_{\ell}}\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Next, denote <math id="A3.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(\alpha_{\ell})=\log\Bigl(\frac{1+e^{-\alpha_{\ell}}-\alpha_{\ell}}{1+e^{-\alpha_{\ell}}}\Bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(\alpha_{\ell})=\log\Bigl(\frac{1+e^{-\alpha_{\ell}}-\alpha_{\ell}}{1+e^{-\alpha_{\ell}}}\Bigr)</annotation></semantics></math>, which is a function of <math id="A3.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus the inequality becomes</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p10" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\sigma_{x_{\ell}}^{2}\geq\log\sigma_{x_{1}}^{2}+\sum_{k=1}^{\ell-1}\left(\frac{1}{\sigma_{x_{k}}+1}+L(\alpha_{\ell})\right)+C." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\sigma_{x_{\ell}}^{2}\geq\log\sigma_{x_{1}}^{2}+\sum_{k=1}^{\ell-1}\left(\frac{1}{\sigma_{x_{k}}+1}+L(\alpha_{\ell})\right)+C.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">For fixed <math id="A3.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{x_{\ell}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{x_{\ell}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\sigma_{x_{\ell}}^{2}\geq L\cdot(C+L(\alpha_{\ell}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\sigma_{x_{\ell}}^{2}\geq L\cdot(C+L(\alpha_{\ell}))</annotation></semantics></math>, if <math id="A3.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{l}&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{l}&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, there is no lower bound for the variance. So it can reach <math id="A3.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>. To establish a upper bound for <math id="A3.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\sigma^{2}_{x_{\ell}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\sigma^{2}_{x_{\ell}}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p12" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k=1}^{\ell-1}\log\Bigl(1+\frac{1}{\sigma_{x_{k}}}\Bigr)\leq\sum_{k=1}^{\ell-1}\frac{1}{\sigma_{x_{k}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k=1}^{\ell-1}\log\Bigl(1+\frac{1}{\sigma_{x_{k}}}\Bigr)\leq\sum_{k=1}^{\ell-1}\frac{1}{\sigma_{x_{k}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">The <math id="A3.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{SiLU}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>SiLU</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{SiLU}</annotation></semantics></math> value of this term is less than or equal to zero (since typically <math id="A3.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\operatorname{SiLU}(\alpha_{\ell})\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>SiLU</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\operatorname{SiLU}(\alpha_{\ell})\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>) or it can be bounded by an appropriate constant <math id="A3.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M(\alpha_{\ell})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(\alpha_{\ell})</annotation></semantics></math>. For our derivation, we denote</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p14" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.E23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\Bigl(1-\operatorname{SiLU}(\alpha_{\ell})\Bigr)\leq M(\alpha_{\ell})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>SiLU</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\Bigl(1-\operatorname{SiLU}(\alpha_{\ell})\Bigr)\leq M(\alpha_{\ell}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">Putting these bounds together we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.E24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\sigma_{x_{\ell}}^{2}\leq\log\sigma_{x_{1}}^{2}+\sum_{k=1}^{\ell-1}\frac{1}{\sigma_{x_{k}}}+M(\alpha_{\ell})+C." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\sigma_{x_{\ell}}^{2}\leq\log\sigma_{x_{1}}^{2}+\sum_{k=1}^{\ell-1}\frac{1}{\sigma_{x_{k}}}+M(\alpha_{\ell})+C.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">Next, we analyze the gradient stability of GPAS. Following Equation (38) in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>]</cite>, and applying the formalization techniques from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">42</a>]</cite>, we derive the result under the consideration that <math id="A3.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{stopgrad}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>stopgrad</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{stopgrad}</annotation></semantics></math> is used, thereby eliminating any gradient contributions at that point. Consequently, we obtain:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p16" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.E25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="UP\left(\left\|\frac{\partial y_{L}}{\partial x_{1}}\right\|_{2}\right)=\prod_{l=1}^{L-1}\left(1+\frac{1}{\sigma_{x_{\ell}}}A+\frac{1}{\sigma_{x_{\ell}}^{2}}B\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">UP\left(\left\|\frac{\partial y_{L}}{\partial x_{1}}\right\|_{2}\right)=\prod_{l=1}^{L-1}\left(1+\frac{1}{\sigma_{x_{\ell}}}A+\frac{1}{\sigma_{x_{\ell}}^{2}}B\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p17" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text">Substitute our lower bound in Equation <a href="#A3.E21" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem of GPAS ‣ GPAS: Accelerating Convergence of LLM Pretraining via Gradient-Preserving Activation Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a> on <math id="A3.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{x_{l}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{x_{l}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> into the above product. Notice that if</span></p>
<table id="A3.E26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{x_{l}}^{2}\geq\sigma_{x_{1}}^{2}\exp\Biggl\{S_{l}\Biggr\}\quad\text{with}\quad S_{l}=\sum_{k=1}^{l-1}\left(\frac{1}{\sigma_{x_{k}}+1}+L(\alpha_{\ell})\right)+C," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>with</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{x_{l}}^{2}\geq\sigma_{x_{1}}^{2}\exp\Biggl\{S_{l}\Biggr\}\quad\text{with}\quad S_{l}=\sum_{k=1}^{l-1}\left(\frac{1}{\sigma_{x_{k}}+1}+L(\alpha_{\ell})\right)+C,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p18" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p18.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p18.1.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, we have the upper bounds on the inverses:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{\sigma_{x_{l}}}\leq\frac{1}{\sigma_{x_{1}}}\exp\Bigl\{-\frac{S_{l}}{2}\Bigr\}\quad\text{and}\quad\frac{1}{\sigma_{x_{l}}^{2}}\leq\frac{1}{\sigma_{x_{1}}^{2}}\exp\Bigl\{-S_{l}\Bigr\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></msub></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{\sigma_{x_{l}}}\leq\frac{1}{\sigma_{x_{1}}}\exp\Bigl\{-\frac{S_{l}}{2}\Bigr\}\quad\text{and}\quad\frac{1}{\sigma_{x_{l}}^{2}}\leq\frac{1}{\sigma_{x_{1}}^{2}}\exp\Bigl\{-S_{l}\Bigr\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p19" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p19.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p19.1.1" class="ltx_text">Thus a valid lower bound for the UP norm is</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p20" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.E28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A3.E28X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E28X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle UP\left(\biggl\|\frac{\partial y_{L}}{\partial x_{1}}\biggr\|_{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle UP\left(\biggl\|\frac{\partial y_{L}}{\partial x_{1}}\biggr\|_{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E28X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\prod_{l=1}^{L-1}\Bigg(1+\frac{A}{\sigma_{x_{1}}}\exp\Bigl\{-\frac{1}{2}\Bigl[\sum_{k=1}^{l-1}\left(\frac{1}{\sigma_{x_{k}}+1}+L(\alpha_{\ell})\right)+C\Bigr]\Bigr\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\prod_{l=1}^{L-1}\Bigg(1+\frac{A}{\sigma_{x_{1}}}\exp\Bigl\{-\frac{1}{2}\Bigl[\sum_{k=1}^{l-1}\left(\frac{1}{\sigma_{x_{k}}+1}+L(\alpha_{\ell})\right)+C\Bigr]\Bigr\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.E28Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E28Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{B}{\sigma_{x_{1}}^{2}}\exp\Bigl\{-\Bigl[\sum_{k=1}^{l-1}\left(\frac{1}{\sigma_{x_{k}}+1}+L(\alpha_{\ell})\right)+C\Bigr]\Bigr\}\Bigg)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>B</mi><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{B}{\sigma_{x_{1}}^{2}}\exp\Bigl\{-\Bigl[\sum_{k=1}^{l-1}\left(\frac{1}{\sigma_{x_{k}}+1}+L(\alpha_{\ell})\right)+C\Bigr]\Bigr\}\Bigg).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p21" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p21.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p21.1.1" class="ltx_text">Similar to above, assuming that for each layer and based on Equation (<a href="#A3.E24" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem of GPAS ‣ GPAS: Accelerating Convergence of LLM Pretraining via Gradient-Preserving Activation Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a>), we have:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p22" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.E29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{x_{\ell}}^{2}\leq\sigma_{x_{1}}^{2}\exp\Biggl\{\sum_{k=1}^{\ell-1}\frac{1}{\sigma_{x_{k}}}+M(\alpha_{\ell})+C\Biggr\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{x_{\ell}}^{2}\leq\sigma_{x_{1}}^{2}\exp\Biggl\{\sum_{k=1}^{\ell-1}\frac{1}{\sigma_{x_{k}}}+M(\alpha_{\ell})+C\Biggr\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p23" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p23.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p23.1.1" class="ltx_text">So we have:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p24" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.E30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{\sigma_{x_{\ell}}}\geq\frac{1}{\sigma_{x_{1}}}\exp\Biggl\{-\frac{1}{2}\Bigl[\sum_{k=1}^{\ell-1}\frac{1}{\sigma_{x_{k}}}+M(\alpha_{\ell})+C\Bigr]\Biggr\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{\sigma_{x_{\ell}}}\geq\frac{1}{\sigma_{x_{1}}}\exp\Biggl\{-\frac{1}{2}\Bigl[\sum_{k=1}^{\ell-1}\frac{1}{\sigma_{x_{k}}}+M(\alpha_{\ell})+C\Bigr]\Biggr\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p25" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p25.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p25.1.1" class="ltx_text">Hence the UP product is upper bounded by</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p26" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.E31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A3.E31X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E31X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle UP\Bigl(\Bigl\|\frac{\partial y_{L}}{\partial x_{1}}\Bigr\|_{2}\Bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle UP\Bigl(\Bigl\|\frac{\partial y_{L}}{\partial x_{1}}\Bigr\|_{2}\Bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E31X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\prod_{\ell=1}^{L-1}\Bigg(1+\frac{A}{\sigma_{x_{1}}}\exp\Biggl\{-\frac{1}{2}\Bigl(\sum_{k=1}^{\ell-1}\frac{1}{\sigma_{x_{k}}}+M(\alpha_{\ell})+C\Bigr)\Biggr\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\prod_{\ell=1}^{L-1}\Bigg(1+\frac{A}{\sigma_{x_{1}}}\exp\Biggl\{-\frac{1}{2}\Bigl(\sum_{k=1}^{\ell-1}\frac{1}{\sigma_{x_{k}}}+M(\alpha_{\ell})+C\Bigr)\Biggr\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.E31Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E31Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{B}{\sigma_{x_{1}}^{2}}\exp\Biggl\{-\Bigl(\sum_{k=1}^{\ell-1}\frac{1}{\sigma_{x_{k}}}+M(\alpha_{\ell})+C\Bigr)\Biggr\}\Bigg])." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>B</mi><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mi>exp</mi><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">]</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{B}{\sigma_{x_{1}}^{2}}\exp\Biggl\{-\Bigl(\sum_{k=1}^{\ell-1}\frac{1}{\sigma_{x_{k}}}+M(\alpha_{\ell})+C\Bigr)\Biggr\}\Bigg]).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Upper bound of <math id="A3.SS1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{UP}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>UP</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{UP}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Assume that the <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M(\alpha_{l})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(\alpha_{l})</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded and will not change so much. Inserting this into (<a href="#A3.E31" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem of GPAS ‣ GPAS: Accelerating Convergence of LLM Pretraining via Gradient-Preserving Activation Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">31</span></a>), thus, in the case of constant <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> and layer-independent <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M(\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain the explicit bound</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.E32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A3.E32X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E32X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle UP\Bigl(\Bigl\|\frac{\partial y_{L}}{\partial x_{1}}\Bigr\|_{2}\Bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle UP\Bigl(\Bigl\|\frac{\partial y_{L}}{\partial x_{1}}\Bigr\|_{2}\Bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E32X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\exp\Biggl\{\frac{A}{\sigma}\exp\Bigl\{-\frac{1}{2}(M(\alpha)+C)\Bigr\}\frac{1-\exp\Bigl\{-\frac{L-1}{2\sigma}\Bigr\}}{1-\exp\Bigl\{-\frac{1}{2\sigma}\Bigr\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>exp</mi><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mi>σ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mi>exp</mi><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\exp\Biggl\{\frac{A}{\sigma}\exp\Bigl\{-\frac{1}{2}(M(\alpha)+C)\Bigr\}\frac{1-\exp\Bigl\{-\frac{L-1}{2\sigma}\Bigr\}}{1-\exp\Bigl\{-\frac{1}{2\sigma}\Bigr\}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.E32Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E32Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{B}{\sigma^{2}}\exp\Bigl\{-\Bigl(M(\alpha)+C\Bigr)\Bigr\}\frac{1-\exp\Bigl\{-\frac{L-1}{\sigma}\Bigr\}}{1-\exp\Bigl\{-\frac{1}{\sigma}\Bigr\}}\Biggr\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>B</mi><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mi>exp</mi><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>σ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>σ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{B}{\sigma^{2}}\exp\Bigl\{-\Bigl(M(\alpha)+C\Bigr)\Bigr\}\frac{1-\exp\Bigl\{-\frac{L-1}{\sigma}\Bigr\}}{1-\exp\Bigl\{-\frac{1}{\sigma}\Bigr\}}\Biggr\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">It is easy to verify:</p>
<table id="A3.E33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1-\exp\Bigl\{-\frac{L-1}{2\sigma}\Bigr\}}{1-\exp\Bigl\{-\frac{1}{2\sigma}\Bigr\}}=O\Bigl(\min\{L,\sigma\}\Bigr)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1-\exp\Bigl\{-\frac{L-1}{2\sigma}\Bigr\}}{1-\exp\Bigl\{-\frac{1}{2\sigma}\Bigr\}}=O\Bigl(\min\{L,\sigma\}\Bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">and similarly</p>
<table id="A3.E34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1-\exp\Bigl\{-\frac{L-1}{\sigma}\Bigr\}}{1-\exp\Bigl\{-\frac{1}{\sigma}\Bigr\}}=O\Bigl(\min\{L,\sigma\}\Bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>σ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>σ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1-\exp\Bigl\{-\frac{L-1}{\sigma}\Bigr\}}{1-\exp\Bigl\{-\frac{1}{\sigma}\Bigr\}}=O\Bigl(\min\{L,\sigma\}\Bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Plug Equations (<a href="#A3.E33" title="In C.1 Upper bound of UP(⋅) ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem of GPAS ‣ GPAS: Accelerating Convergence of LLM Pretraining via Gradient-Preserving Activation Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">33</span></a>) and (<a href="#A3.E34" title="In C.1 Upper bound of UP(⋅) ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem of GPAS ‣ GPAS: Accelerating Convergence of LLM Pretraining via Gradient-Preserving Activation Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">34</span></a>) into the bound. We deduce</p>
<table id="A3.E35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A3.E35X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E35X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle UP\Bigl(\Bigl\|\frac{\partial y_{L}}{\partial x_{1}}\Bigr\|_{2}\Bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle UP\Bigl(\Bigl\|\frac{\partial y_{L}}{\partial x_{1}}\Bigr\|_{2}\Bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="4" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.E35Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E35Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\exp\Biggl\{\frac{A}{\sigma}\exp\Bigl\{-\frac{1}{2}(M(\alpha)+C)\Bigr\}O\bigl(\min\{L,\sigma\}\bigr)+\frac{B}{\sigma^{2}}\exp\Bigl\{-(M(\alpha)+C)\Bigr\}O\bigl(\min\{L,\sigma\}\bigr)\Biggr\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mi>σ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>exp</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>B</mi><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>exp</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\exp\Biggl\{\frac{A}{\sigma}\exp\Bigl\{-\frac{1}{2}(M(\alpha)+C)\Bigr\}O\bigl(\min\{L,\sigma\}\bigr)+\frac{B}{\sigma^{2}}\exp\Bigl\{-(M(\alpha)+C)\Bigr\}O\bigl(\min\{L,\sigma\}\bigr)\Biggr\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.E35Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E35Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\exp\Biggl\{O\Biggl(\frac{A}{\sigma}\exp\Bigl\{-\frac{1}{2}(M(\alpha)+C)\Bigr\}\min\{L,\sigma\}\Biggr)+O\Biggl(\frac{B}{\sigma^{2}}\exp\Bigl\{-(M(\alpha)+C)\Bigr\}\min\{L,\sigma\}\Biggr)\Biggr\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mi>σ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>exp</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>min</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>B</mi><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>exp</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>min</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\exp\Biggl\{O\Biggl(\frac{A}{\sigma}\exp\Bigl\{-\frac{1}{2}(M(\alpha)+C)\Bigr\}\min\{L,\sigma\}\Biggr)+O\Biggl(\frac{B}{\sigma^{2}}\exp\Bigl\{-(M(\alpha)+C)\Bigr\}\min\{L,\sigma\}\Biggr)\Biggr\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.E35Xc" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E35Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\exp\left\{O\Biggl(\exp\Bigl\{-\frac{1}{2}(M(\alpha))\Bigr\}\frac{\min\{L,\sigma\}}{\sigma}\Biggr)\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>σ</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\exp\left\{O\Biggl(\exp\Bigl\{-\frac{1}{2}(M(\alpha))\Bigr\}\frac{\min\{L,\sigma\}}{\sigma}\Biggr)\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Lower bound for <math id="A3.SS2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{UP}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>UP</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{UP}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Assume that the <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(\alpha_{l})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(\alpha_{l})</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded and will not change so much. Inserting this into (<a href="#A3.E28" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem of GPAS ‣ GPAS: Accelerating Convergence of LLM Pretraining via Gradient-Preserving Activation Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a>), thus, in the case of constant <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> and layer-independent <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M(\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math>, we can obtain the explicit bound.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Assume with <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D=\frac{1}{\sigma+1}+L_{(}\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo></msub><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=\frac{1}{\sigma+1}+L_{(}\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math>, For each term in the product (with index <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math>), define</p>
<table id="A3.E36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(l)=1+\frac{A}{\sigma}\exp\Bigl\{-\frac{1}{2}\Bigl[(l-1)D+C\Bigr]\Bigr\}+\frac{B}{\sigma^{2}}\exp\Bigl\{-\Bigl[(l-1)D+C\Bigr]\Bigr\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mi>σ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>B</mi><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(l)=1+\frac{A}{\sigma}\exp\Bigl\{-\frac{1}{2}\Bigl[(l-1)D+C\Bigr]\Bigr\}+\frac{B}{\sigma^{2}}\exp\Bigl\{-\Bigl[(l-1)D+C\Bigr]\Bigr\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Taking the logarithm of the whole product, we get</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.E37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{s=0}^{L-2}\Biggl\{\frac{A}{\sigma}\exp\Bigl\{-\frac{1}{2}(sD+C)\Bigr\}+\frac{B}{\sigma^{2}}\exp\Bigl\{-\bigl(sD+C\bigr)\Bigr\}+O\Bigl(\exp\{-sD-C\}\Bigr)\Biggr\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mi>σ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>B</mi><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{s=0}^{L-2}\Biggl\{\frac{A}{\sigma}\exp\Bigl\{-\frac{1}{2}(sD+C)\Bigr\}+\frac{B}{\sigma^{2}}\exp\Bigl\{-\bigl(sD+C\bigr)\Bigr\}+O\Bigl(\exp\{-sD-C\}\Bigr)\Biggr\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Each of the sums over <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> is a geometric series. For instance,</p>
<table id="A3.E38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E38.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sum_{s=0}^{L-2}\exp\Bigl\{-\frac{1}{2}(sD+C)\Bigr\}=e^{-C/2}\sum_{s=0}^{L-2}\left(e^{-D/2}\right)^{s}=e^{-C/2}\frac{1-e^{-(L-1)D/2}}{1-e^{-D/2}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></munderover><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mi>D</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></munderover><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{s=0}^{L-2}\exp\Bigl\{-\frac{1}{2}(sD+C)\Bigr\}=e^{-C/2}\sum_{s=0}^{L-2}\left(e^{-D/2}\right)^{s}=e^{-C/2}\frac{1-e^{-(L-1)D/2}}{1-e^{-D/2}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p">and similarly for the second term. Notice that when <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="e^{-D/2}&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{-D/2}&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math> the whole sum (even as <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>) is bounded by a constant. Exponentiating, we can write:</p>
<table id="A3.E39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E39.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="UP\Bigl(\Bigl\|\frac{\partial y_{L}}{\partial x_{1}}\Bigr\|_{2}\Bigr)\geq\exp\Biggl\{\frac{A}{\sigma}e^{-C/2}\frac{1}{1-e^{-D/2}}+\frac{B}{\sigma^{2}}e^{-C}\frac{1}{1-e^{-D}}+O(1)\Biggr\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.600em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><msub><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.600em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mi>σ</mi></mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>B</mi><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msup><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">UP\Bigl(\Bigl\|\frac{\partial y_{L}}{\partial x_{1}}\Bigr\|_{2}\Bigr)\geq\exp\Biggl\{\frac{A}{\sigma}e^{-C/2}\frac{1}{1-e^{-D/2}}+\frac{B}{\sigma^{2}}e^{-C}\frac{1}{1-e^{-D}}+O(1)\Biggr\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">similar to the above process, we can get:</p>
<table id="A3.E40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="UP\Bigl(\Bigl\|\frac{\partial y_{L}}{\partial x_{1}}\Bigr\|_{2}\Bigr)\geq\exp\Bigg\{O\Bigg(\frac{1}{\sigma}\frac{1}{1-e^{(-\frac{1}{\sigma+1}+L(\alpha))/2}}+1\Bigg)\Biggr\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>σ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">UP\Bigl(\Bigl\|\frac{\partial y_{L}}{\partial x_{1}}\Bigr\|_{2}\Bigr)\geq\exp\Bigg\{O\Bigg(\frac{1}{\sigma}\frac{1}{1-e^{(-\frac{1}{\sigma+1}+L(\alpha))/2}}+1\Bigg)\Biggr\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p6.2" class="ltx_p">∎</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>License</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We provide licenses of assets used in our paper, including model, dataset and code.</p>
<ul id="A4.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">C4 dataset: This is the dataset we used in our pretraining experiments. It’s released under the <a href="https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/by/1-0/" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_href">Open Data Commons License Attribution family License</a>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Commonsense 170K dataset: This is the dataset we used for supervised fine-tuning, released under <a href="https://choosealicense.com/licenses/mit/" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_href">MIT License</a>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
</article>
</div>
</div>
